  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 requires serious incident reporting within 24h and other confirmed incidents within 10 business days (14 days), with customer notice within 5 business days (7 days); scope is limited to confirmed incidents. S2 keeps a 55°C test and 5% threshold but allows continued sales above 5% with corrective action and retesting, and gives per-model numeric results to buyers but not the public. S3 requires new-unit shut-off and a 6-year retrofit window; S4 requires built-in suppression after 36 months; S5 mandates recall at 8/100k with prompt notice and no transition."
